Error [jet.WebBoundaryTypeNotAllowed]: `Point` cannot cross the JS/WASM boundary on a `#Export(wasm)` parameter
  --> tests/ui/web_abi_type.jet:7:1
    |
  7 | export_bad: fn(p: Point) -> Int { p.x }
    | ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Web exports and imports only admit ABI-safe types (scalars, `String`, lists and maps of ABI-safe values, and `#Codable` structs/enums)
 Fix: Use a scalar, `String`, a list or map of ABI-safe values, or a `#Codable` struct/enum whose fields are ABI-safe
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-WEB-ABI-TYPE
